WEBVTT

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.000
♬ I'll go with you ♬

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.090
Thank you for your kind attention!

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.840
That video was from five years ago.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.430
As you just saw,

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.890
I have been operating till now
in order to fulfill my mission

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:38.230
of making everyone happy
with my singing.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.560
Mainly at a place called NiaLand.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.440
Really? I've never heard of it!

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:43.480
I've never heard of it, either.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.770
I've been, but I didn't see you there.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.230
Now, now, settle down.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.570
You should know she was very famous!

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.320
Here, at the AI Museum--

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.240
Hey! Sing something, will you?

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.870
I am sorry, but that won't be--

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.330
Oh?

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.130
Come on, don't put her on the spot.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.960
It's time to move on,
so let's all thank her, class.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.630
Okay...

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:11.470
--Thanks!
--Bye!

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:16.470
66 years--

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Osamu!

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.070
--Hurry up!
--Come on, let's go!

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.870
Tour program, complete.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:38.080
Please return to the
specified coordinates, and stand by.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.360
Well, that's a woeful face
if I've ever seen one!

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:13.070
I would never guess you were
the same person as the one in that video!

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:19.950
<i>AS YOU LIKE MY PLEASURE</i>

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:35.380
<i>I was born aiming for the light</i>

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:41.310
<i>Bound by a bond,</i>
<i>a thin string</i>

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:46.310
<i>From the fortune of</i>
<i>awakening for a mission</i>

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:53.110
<i>Spinning many proud memories</i>

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.990
<i>Into this world,</i>
<i>for your sake</i>

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:05.410
<i>Gratitude and a bouquet filled</i>
<i>with the universe</i>

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:11.590
<i>Destiny, even fate,</i>
<i>please let them shine</i>

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:16.550
<i>The joy of being able to protect those</i>
<i>having fun and smiling</i>

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:19.930
<i>I admire,</i>
<i>I am admiring</i>

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.510
<i>I can become stronger</i>

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:27.810
<i>I want even my crying voice</i>
<i>to be heard like a song</i>

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:32.780
<i>To these dazzling times</i>

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:42.280
<i>I'd like you to entrust tears too</i>

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:49.540
EPISODE 10

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:49.540
VIVY SCORE -
SINGING FROM MY HEART

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.330
Matsumoto.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.960
It is indeed I,
after five years--forgive me!

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:52.130
Making it 45 years and
six months since we last met?

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:55.510
I have been waiting for you all
this time! What do I have to do next--

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.720
Hmm? What's going on with you?

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:02.100
The Singularity Project
is all that I have now--

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.600
I see, so that's what this is about.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.140
You've retired, I hear?

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.520
The original songstress AI, Diva, retires.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.480
I hear the ceremony was
quite the extravaganza.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:18.860
Although the fans weren't happy about
being deprived of a farewell concert.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.620
After retiring, you were donated
to this AI Museum,

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.410
where you serve as an exhibit.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:29.370
But no one has ever heard you sing.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.880
Have you... lost the ability to sing?

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.050
Even now, I'm not sure.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.590
How I can pour my heart into my singing.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:46.100
Even though I'm supposed to make
everyone happy with my singing.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:52.020
Like Diva that day...

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:56.570
Once that thought crossed my mind,
I found myself unable to sing anymore.

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:57.480
That is why I only--

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.570
Unfortunately, you can no longer
work on the Singularity Project.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:02.570
Why not?

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:05.120
There is nothing wrong with me
except for the singing! Even my body is--

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:06.700
The reason being...

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:12.330
The incident with Ophelia turned out to be
the final anticipated Singularity Point.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:16.920
Do you know about
Ophelia's double suicide?

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.800
Yes, I know.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:23.140
About the uproar that followed, too,

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:26.720
when people claimed that they both
had souls just like humans.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.890
How is that different
from the original history?

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.220
Even so...

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.430
Unlike in the original timeline,

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.690
there were no AIs
who followed their example.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:34.730
In hindsight, there's no denying

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:37.690
that it was a positive revision
in terms of the project.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.150
Our job correcting
the Singularity Points is done.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:45.530
But if that is the case,
why did you not go into sleep mode?

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.370
What happened to "no altering
history unnecessarily"?

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.660
Hmm...

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:59.090
Something Mr. Kakitani said
has been bugging me.

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:03.050
Through a revelation.
A revelation from the heavens.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:06.890
Not to mention,
I have a personal favor to fulfill.

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.390
A favor?

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:11.350
For you to be concerned about
something other than your mission...

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:12.520
Well, who are you to talk?

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:13.350
Singing was your sole devotion,

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.480
yet here you are,
championing the Singularity Project,

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:18.360
which you're starting to see
as your mainstay, no less?

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.610
Well, not that there's anything
you can do anymore.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.910
Would you like to race me, perhaps?

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.240
Race you?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:32.660
To see who can accomplish
their respective task first.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.370
That does not sound like you.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:38.630
But I have no idea what I must do
to find an answer.

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:42.380
Even though I can never
set foot on stage again.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.590
"Pour your heart into your singing."

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.720
Why would my developer say such a thing?

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:52.770
Well, the only way you're going to find
out is by asking your developer herself.

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:55.770
Vivy?

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:58.940
Hmm...

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.020
Well, you just keep on pondering, okay?

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.240
I mean, you've got
nothing but time, right?

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.030
I'll pop in again sometime
to check on you.

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:07.070
Come to think of it...

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:09.740
Why did you choose today
to come see me?

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:12.620
Have you forgotten?

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:16.790
It was 65 years ago today.

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.080
The day that you and I first met.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.670
Can you think of
a better date for a reunion?

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:27.890
We will be closing soon.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:30.430
We will be looking forward
to your next visit.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.690
Normal access detected.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:47.320
Welcome to the AI
aggregate database, The Archive.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.040
Is there still data from
my manufacturer and rollout date?

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.750
Yes. Would you like me to display it?

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:02.500
Please do.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:03.960
Understood.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:10.050
Now displaying data
from June 19, 2060, 22:01.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.850
"Sing from her heart"?

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:20.060
Now why would you give her
such a complex task?

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.730
Because I'm looking for a hint.

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:25.070
Excuse me... a hint?

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:31.120
What is a heart,
as it applies to us humans?

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:36.080
As the first autonomous humanoid AI,
I'm curious as to what her answer will be.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:38.210
That's what I'm looking forward to.

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:41.460
That's not what we're
looking for in this project.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:43.710
I'm not sure that adding
an ambiguous term like "heart"

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:45.380
to her computing process--

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:47.840
It doesn't matter how it turns out.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:50.840
Even if having a heart in her own way...

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:54.100
...leads her to resent us humans,
I'd have no problem with that.

00:08:55.310 --> 00:09:00.850
Now then... I wonder what kind of
singing she's going to treat us to?

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:12.450
Your mission is to make
everyone happy with your singing.

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:16.950
To accomplish that,
you must sing from your heart.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:20.410
Um... um, excuse me?

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:27.000
Please forgive me.
How may I help you?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.130
Um...

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:32.380
Your name is Osamu, correct?

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.850
You were here yesterday on a field trip.

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:35.850
How did you--

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:38.350
That is what your teacher called you.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:45.270
Um... so did you retire because
you couldn't sing anymore?

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:47.900
Um...

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:50.690
You were the first-ever songstress AI,

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:53.450
and you were popular,
so why did you retire?

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:56.700
That was the only reason I could think of.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.870
Are you saying that you knew about me
despite being so young, Osamu?

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.500
That's just common sense.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:06.540
My classmates not knowing about you--
that's what's messed up.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.210
You are correct.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:13.760
I am here now because I found myself
unable to sing anymore.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:16.850
Not even one song?
Even though it's your mission to sing?

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.970
Yes.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:25.060
I really wanted to hear you
sing in person, Diva.

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:26.520
I am sorry.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:34.360
In that case, Osamu...
would you like to race me?

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:36.030
Race you?

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:40.120
I am searching for answers
as to what it is I must do...

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:43.160
...to be able to sing again.

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:45.460
Will I find the answer first,

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:49.670
or will you bring some friends here first?

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:53.170
B-But I don't really care
about friends, you know--

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.130
Right. I am aware of that.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:57.510
But will you still accept the challenge?

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:01.470
As having someone to compete with
will help me to try harder.

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.140
Okay.

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:05.890
Thank you very much.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:16.200
Um, can I come again
even without any friends?

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.360
Of course you can.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:20.280
I look forward to your next visit.

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:39.510
Not even a single song?

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:44.480
When I used to be able
to sing over a million existing songs...

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.310
Could this be more pathetic?

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:53.860
Archive?

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:54.690
Yes?

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:57.950
Are there any songs written
by AIs in the past?

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:00.160
I have found more than 100,000 songs.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:01.490
Would you like to look over them?

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:05.910
No. Not songs that humans
had composer AIs or bots write.

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:09.170
Are there any that were written by AIs
of their own free will?

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.840
No such songs exist.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:15.340
I see.

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:24.140
Long time no see!

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:27.890
What are you doing there?

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:36.820
Since I could not find any existing songs
in my drive that I can sing now,

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:40.490
I thought that if I wrote
one myself, then maybe--

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:42.120
How simplistic!

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:45.240
Don't tell me that's what you've
been doing for a whole year?

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:47.330
What kind of song is it, by the way?

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:01.840
Wait, you can't be serious!

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:02.930
Please tell me there's
more to it than that!

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:04.640
Would you please shut up?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:10.060
What this song is about... Who I am
going to sing it for... I have no idea.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.310
Wouldn't you say you're making
a headlong rush into a dead end?

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.360
At this rate, there's no telling
when you'll be done.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:16.070
Or whether you'll be able to
sing it if you do finish it.

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:20.780
What about you? You have not
taken care of that favor yet, have you?

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:24.160
Well, I would advise you not to overdo it.

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:28.250
Impossible. I must try anything
and everything to fulfill my mission.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:30.830
Taking such a roundabout route
will only get you so far, I'm afraid.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.790
Well, I'll drop by again
when the time comes.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.590
Like next year, maybe.

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:38.050
Yes. See you next year,
on the day we met.

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:32.790
Diva?

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:37.620
Osamu?

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.380
Have you found your answer?

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:42.590
No. Nothing has changed.

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:43.630
I see.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.300
I am sorry. I should try harder--

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:49.930
No, I'm not judging you
or anything. It's just that...

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:53.140
I feel sad not being able to help you.

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:55.680
What is her name?

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:59.770
It's Luna. She's partly named
after my wife Nana, see.

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:00.810
Little Luna?

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:02.270
Want to hold her?

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:03.730
Are you sure?

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:12.990
Why do you think Nana was able to smile?

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:15.540
When surely no one wanted
to see this child grow up...

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:16.960
...more than her.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:21.670
I don't know. But she did tell me
how much she was looking forward to it.

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:26.340
Seeing what path this child would take,

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:30.890
what would make her laugh, make her cry,
and what kind of people she would meet.

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:35.770
Diva...

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:39.310
All humans die one day.

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:42.230
But they all remain inside someone,
no matter what.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.860
My wife is still here inside me, even now.

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:52.700
I'm going to leave it all to you.

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:04.340
So I'm going to see it through to the end.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:10.300
Normal access detected.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:14.220
Welcome to the AI
aggregate database, The Archive.

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:43.940
Is this song... would it be
the Singularity Project, by any chance?

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:45.520
Yes.

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:47.110
That explains it...

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:51.490
I don't know what came over me,
but I forgot myself while listening to it.

00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:53.700
Why choose to write about the project?

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:55.660
I thought that if it was about
the path I have taken,

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:57.870
and who I have met until now...

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:00.410
...then I might be able to
come up with a song.

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:04.370
A song about yourself, then?

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.670
Who did you write it for?

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:11.550
It is for Diva.
Although she is gone now...

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:13.720
...she still remains inside me.

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:16.090
She is part of me.

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:20.640
And? You think that this song will
enable you to sing from your heart?

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:25.140
If I could sing,
I would have sung it already.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:26.400
Seriously...

00:19:26.400 --> 00:19:29.310
I have to say, for someone
stuck on a single phrase for years,

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:32.110
you sure cranked it out all in one go!

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:34.030
Did something trigger that, perhaps?

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:38.160
Someone gripped my finger.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:39.240
Excuse me?

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.750
It has been a year, right, Matsumoto?

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:44.620
Sorry to do this to you
when you came to see me...

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.080
...but I am going to sleep a bit.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.170
Huh?

00:19:47.170 --> 00:19:48.830
For some reason, I feel sleepy.

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:49.920
See you next year.

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:50.790
Hey!

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:57.630
Do not worry... I will wake up
if any visitors come.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:02.140
Well, you did just finish the task you've
been burdened with for 20 years.

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:06.100
I suppose your computing circuits
need some respite, too, eh?

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:10.440
I've fulfilled my promise, Diva.

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:12.860
Well, not that Vivy
could've sung it, either,

00:20:12.860 --> 00:20:16.570
so I guess we'll have to
put the results of our race on hold.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.490
Good night, Vivy.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.700
I hope our paths will
cross again someday...

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:27.660
...in a future where there's no war.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:35.050
Diva?

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:44.220
Music data?

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:57.360
I see.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:58.780
So you've done it.

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:03.740
Good work, Diva.

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.870
I want you to take it easy for now.

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:09.370
The next time you wake up,
I'm sure I'll get to hear your voice--

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:11.290
Mr. Matsumoto? Excuse me--

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.250
Right, I'm on my way.

00:23:46.240 --> 00:23:48.120
Please hold on a second!
What is going on--

